---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout title="About Numlore" description="A bidirectional dictionary for numbers and the words they mean.">
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-[color:var(--hairline)] pb-2">
    <span class="label">Colophon</span>
    <span class="label">About</span>
  </div>

  <header class="mt-10">
    <h1 class="text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight md:text-6xl">About</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-3">A field guide to the meanings of numbers.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="entry mt-14">
    <div class="entry-label label">What</div>
    <div class="entry-value max-w-prose">
      Numlore is a bidirectional number↔word mnemonic dictionary. Type a number to see its cultural references, Major System mnemonics, T9 keypad letters, and leet readings. Type a word to find the numbers it encodes to.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="entry mt-6">
    <div class="entry-label label">How</div>
    <div class="entry-value max-w-prose">
      Curated entries are written by hand. Notable numbers — years, repdigits, palindromes, well-known codes — are auto-flagged at build time. Everything else is rendered algorithmically on demand at the edge.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="entry mt-6">
    <div class="entry-label label">Privacy</div>
    <div class="entry-value max-w-prose">
      We don't record individual choices that can be mapped back to a person. Aggregate page hits via Glyphex are the only telemetry. The full posture is on <a class="u" href="/privacy">/privacy</a>.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="entry mt-6">
    <div class="entry-label label">Made by</div>
    <div class="entry-value max-w-prose">
      Numlore is a Skadi Oy property. Helsinki.
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
